ProsperoSunshine: end the session app with the last client on the PS5

Upstream keeps the app and its gamepads for a later resume. On the PS5 the virtual pads would keep
taking over the console user's input with no client connected.

--- a/src/stream.cpp
+++ b/src/stream.cpp
@@ -2251,6 +2251,11 @@
 
       // If this is the last session, invoke the platform callbacks
       if (--running_sessions == 0) {
+#ifdef __SCE__
+        // "PS5 Screen" has nothing to pause: the console keeps running without a client. Ending it here
+        // also removes the virtual pads, which would otherwise take over the console user's input.
+        proc::proc.terminate();
+#endif
         bool revert_display_config {config::video.dd.config_revert_on_disconnect};
         if (proc::proc.running()) {
 #if defined SUNSHINE_TRAY && SUNSHINE_TRAY >= 1
